---
layout: manifesto
footer: The pour-over problem
---
:: kick ::
The problem with the old way
:: title ::
The big chains are built for machines, not for mornings.
:: note ::
Industrial espresso is a vat of bitter, over-extracted XML — engineered for throughput, not for taste. Order a deck from it and what lands is misaligned, off-brand, lukewarm. So you spend the "saved" hour fixing the foam by hand.
